WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:06.210
The most unique thing about Tijuana’s biggest
shelter for the so called Caravan migrants

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.840
is
that it provides hardly any shelter at all

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:13.949
– at least not from the elements, not from
the rain, and not from the cold during freezing

00:00:13.949 --> 00:00:18.130
nights.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:24.330
Designated by city officials to hold a maximum
of just 2500 people, this place now houses

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:26.640
more than 6000 migrants.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.640
And in a few days that number will swell further
to 7,000, including more than one thousand

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:36.840
babies, toddlers and young children.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.039
We meet Cindy Pinera again.

00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:42.829
When we talked to her about a week ago, she
had just arrived with two of her four sisters

00:00:42.829 --> 00:00:44.180
and without her father.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.920
The family had gotten separated on their journey
to Tijuana.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:52.500
Now, they are reunited, but conditions here
have dramatically deteriorated…

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.050
We’re in really bad shape.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.500
As you can see everything is wet.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.929
We are tired, we couldn't get any sleep last
night.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:06.090
It's hard when the babies are all wet.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:09.300
It’s getting worse for us with no real place
to stay.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:14.260
This tent is not even mine.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:19.210
The city of Tijuana, some state agencies and
an increasing number of NGOs are doing what

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.800
they can to cope with the situation.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.600
Infections and diseases are on the rise, head
lice are a problem, overall hygiene is a major

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.600
concern.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.930
Tijuana’s mayor says he is battling what
he calls an “unprecedented humanitarian

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:34.510
crisis” in his town.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:37.960
– with almost NO help from the central government
in Mexico City.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:56.740
It’s people we’re dealing with…who’s
going to be responsible?

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:01.670
Mexico City has finally sent more federal
police and some military to Tijuana.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:06.450
But that doesn’t solve the city’s financial
problems, as it spends almost $30,000 dollars

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.520
a day on its migrant crisis.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.229
A fortune for the border town.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:21.640
If you know someone who wants to help… here
in this office.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:23.590
Tijuana - Help Wanted!

